# --- managed by github-actions-align: regenerated on apply; add your own BELOW the end marker ---
# Goes at the BUILD CONTEXT root, not beside the Dockerfile. Rationale: github-actions-align/templates/README.md#dockerignore

# Version control — biggest context bloat and a real leak risk
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Dependencies and build output — rebuilt inside the image
node_modules
vendor
target
__pycache__
.venv
venv
bin
dist
coverage

# Tooling and CI config the image never needs
.golangci.yml
.yamllint.yml
.hadolint.yaml
ruff.toml
eslint.config.mjs
taskfile.yml
.taskfiles
Makefile
renovate.json
release-please-config.json
.release-please-manifest.json

# Docs and local junk
docs
*.md
!README.md
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.worktrees
.idea
.vscode

# Test fixtures.
# CAUTION: delete these two lines if this repo's Dockerfile runs `go mod tidy` —
# tidy computes requirements from the whole module INCLUDING tests, so stripping
# *_test.go changes what it resolves.
**/testdata
**/*_test.go
# --- end managed ---

# More info: https://docs.docker.com/engine/reference/builder/#dockerignore-file
# Ignore everything by default and re-include only needed files
**

# Podman/buildah does not descend into a directory excluded by `**` for the
# `!**/*.go` pattern below (buildah#6417), so re-include the source trees by name.
!cmd
!api
!internal

# Re-include Go source files (but not *_test.go)
!**/*.go
**/*_test.go
# The re-included trees may hold fixtures (e.g. internal/authentik/testdata).
**/testdata

# Re-include Go module files
!go.mod
!go.sum
